---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';
import { loadSizes } from '../data/business';
---

<Layout
  title="How Junk Removal Pricing Works"
  description="Understand how volume, materials, access, and disposal requirements affect a junk removal estimate in Lancaster County. No invented prices or surprise assumptions."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Pricing', url: '/pricing' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">KNOW WHAT GOES INTO THE COST</p>
      <h1>
        A clear estimate.
        <br />A simpler decision.
      </h1>
      <p>
        No two piles are quite the same. The best place to start is with what
        you have and where it needs to come from.
      </p>
      <CTA />
    </section>
    <section class="content-grid page-content">
      <div>
        <h2>Four things shape the estimate.</h2>
        <ol class="plain-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Volume.</strong> How much room the items take up in a load.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Materials.</strong> Heavy debris and special-handling items
            can differ from ordinary household clutter.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Labor and access.</strong> Stairs, distance to the truck,
            tight doors, and disassembly affect the work.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Disposal requirements.</strong> The type of material
            determines which handling options are appropriate.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <h2>Photos are a useful starting point.</h2>
        <p>
          Take a wide photo of the items together, then another of the access
          route. Mention anything not visible, such as upstairs items or an
          appliance connection. An on-site look may be needed to confirm the
          scope.
        </p>
        <h2>Thinking in load sizes</h2>
        <p>
          We’re considering load-based pricing. These are planning categories,
          not published rates or guaranteed truck capacities.
        </p>
        <div class="load-sizes">
          {loadSizes.map((s) => (
            <span>{s}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p>
          Actual prices and the final pricing model will be added here once
          confirmed. You’ll need an estimate for your specific job.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="callout">
        <h2>Help us see the whole picture.</h2>
        <p>
          Include your item list, ZIP, photos if you have them, and any stairs
          or access limitations. Tell us your timing, too.
        </p>
        <p>There’s no need to guess how much truck space you’ll need.</p>
        <CTA />
      </aside>
    </section>
    <div class="section">
      <FinalCTA />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
